{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1160960-who-else-would-love-to-see-dark-age-wraith-dark-age-mummy-become-a-reality","id":1160960,"title":"Who else would love to see Dark Age: Wraith & Dark Age: Mummy become a reality?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-20T13:49:25-08:00","id":1160960,"title":"Who else would love to see Dark Age: Wraith & Dark Age: Mummy become a reality?","content":"I love the Dark Age line, with all of it's qualities and Flaws.<br /> <br /> Obviously, the big 3 (Vampire, Werewolf and Mage) made it with, relatively, little change. Changeling and Hunter, we're altered a bit more, but I love those 2 lines (better in a way than the original game)...although I was sadden that Dark Age: Fae never got its Player's Guide (maybe an idea for a Changeling 20th anniversary book). Although softcover, <i>Blood &amp; Silk</i> and <i>Devil's Due</i> were an interesting adaptation of Kindred of the East and Demon the Fallen respectively.<br /> <br /> sadly 2 of my Favorite lines Wraith and Mummy never got the chance to be adapted or get a Dark Age treatment (even as a softcover). But there would be so much to explore when you think of it:<br /> <br /> How would be the Shadowland between the 1st and 2nd Great Maelstrom? Back then, the 3 forbidden Guilds were also active. How did this affect the dynamic of the land? How did plagues, famine, war and higher Infantile mortality affect the population and the Legions? To cover but a few topic. Maybe this could be looked into as a Wraith 20th Anniversary supplement.<br /> <br /> For Mummy, do they stick to their traditional boundary of Egypt (Modern day Egypt and Soudan) are travel around the Mediterranean? How about Bog Mummies from the British Isles and Northen Europe? How do they feel about the Arabic/Muslim rulers? Are they seen as being transitory like the Greek, Roman and Byzantine Rulers were? And the other supernatural (Vampire (Setite and Assamite mostly) and Shapeshifter (Garou, Mokole and Bastet mostly)) how are they perceived? Not too sure how it would get published, but still would love to have it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":3226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","user":"Boneguard","date":". 11-21-2017, 05:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T14:14:37-08:00","id":1160965,"title":"","content":"I think about a dozen years ago, I wrote up a pitch for Dark Ages: Wraith, which would've focused on relatively younger restless dead still tied to the Skinlands from between the 6th century and the 13th century &quot;present&quot;, who were largely unaware of Stygia and any of it's problems or politics, instead being completely focused on their own small forts, castles, towns and cities and surviving day to day existence as restless dead. To them, this is Purgatory, where they have to purge themselves of their sins before being worthy of Heaven, and if they happen to come across Stygian wraiths, those are clearly denizens of Limbo who may wish to drag them down into hell. It would've been a medieval gothic low-fantasy setting, with knights and priests and bandits and what have you, where the people have to occasionally deal with freakish demonic monsters (specters and such) as well as their own moral weaknesses (Shadows). Sort of like Army of Darkness with more psychodrama and less slapstick. And it's a society that would've been entirely swept away when the Great Maelstrom of the Black Plague hit.<br /> Of course, this entire thing was just an intellectual exercise, as it was well after End of Empire and there was no chance of any new Wraith material back then. <br /> <br /> As far as Mummy goes, I think you're going to have a lot of diaspora during the Ptolemaic and Roman periods, with them spreading into Persia, Greece, the rest of the Mediterranean, and up into Gaul and Britain (and even down into Ethiopia) before the Dark Ages, so in theory they could pop up almost anywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T15:01:22-08:00","id":1160975,"title":"","content":"Dark Agees was the absolute peak of WoD and I\u2019m devastated that we never got to see Wraith for it. While I wouldn\u2019t buy it now, I\u2019d be distantly pleased if it ever did come out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T15:50:17-08:00","id":1160993,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1160960-who-else-would-love-to-see-dark-age-wraith-dark-age-mummy-become-a-reality?p=1160965#post1160965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think about a dozen years ago, I wrote up a pitch for Dark Ages: Wraith, which would've focused on relatively younger restless dead still tied to the Skinlands from between the 6th century and the 13th century &quot;present&quot;, who were largely unaware of Stygia and any of it's problems or politics, instead being completely focused on their own small forts, castles, towns and cities and surviving day to day existence as restless dead. To them, this is Purgatory, where they have to purge themselves of their sins before being worthy of Heaven, and if they happen to come across Stygian wraiths, those are clearly denizens of Limbo who may wish to drag them down into hell. It would've been a medieval gothic low-fantasy setting, with knights and priests and bandits and what have you, where the people have to occasionally deal with freakish demonic monsters (specters and such) as well as their own moral weaknesses (Shadows). Sort of like Army of Darkness with more psychodrama and less slapstick. And it's a society that would've been entirely swept away when the Great Maelstrom of the Black Plague hit.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1160960-who-else-would-love-to-see-dark-age-wraith-dark-age-mummy-become-a-reality?p=1160965#post1160965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Of course, this entire thing was just an intellectual exercise, as it was well after End of Empire and there was no chance of any new Wraith material back then.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Now that is an interesting take to it. I like it a lot as it would make a lot of sense for the Shadowlands to have it's own Dark age with a &quot;collapse&quot; (so to speak) of the Empire. And the Christian spin to it would also make sense under that lense.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1160960-who-else-would-love-to-see-dark-age-wraith-dark-age-mummy-become-a-reality?p=1160965#post1160965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">As far as Mummy goes, I think you're going to have a lot of diaspora during the Ptolemaic and Roman periods, with them spreading into Persia, Greece, the rest of the Mediterranean, and up into Gaul and Britain (and even down into Ethiopia) before the Dark Ages, so in theory they could pop up almost anywhere. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I had not thought of this, but it is a fair point. There was a possibility of a lot of movement under the Roman Empire and the Mummy could have taken advantage of it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1160960-who-else-would-love-to-see-dark-age-wraith-dark-age-mummy-become-a-reality?p=1160975#post1160975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dark Agees was the absolute peak of WoD and I\u2019m devastated that we never got to see Wraith for it. While I wouldn\u2019t buy it now, I\u2019d be distantly pleased if it ever did come out.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fair point. After so many years, make sense that people moved on. Although I'm glad to see that I,m not the only one who thinks Dark Ages was Great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":3226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","user":"Boneguard","date":". 11-20-2017, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T17:06:25-08:00","id":1161010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boneguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1160960-who-else-would-love-to-see-dark-age-wraith-dark-age-mummy-become-a-reality?p=1160993#post1160993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a fair point. After so many years, make sense that people moved on. Although I'm glad to see that I,m not the only one who thinks Dark Ages was Great.</div> </div> </div> </div>I enjoy the line quite a bit, especially the period when Rich Dansky was developer. The book I really wish had been done was The Ashen Lady, talking about women in the medieval period from real world/dark medieval as well as vampire and other supernatural perspectives, because the real role of women in that period is way more interesting than the post-Victorian public perception of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T21:28:22-08:00","id":1161083,"title":"","content":"I would so be for a Dark Ages Wraith. Seeing the guilds being active and Charon still be around are the most interesting concepts for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T16:46:51-08:00","id":1161334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1160960-who-else-would-love-to-see-dark-age-wraith-dark-age-mummy-become-a-reality?p=1161083#post1161083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would so be for a Dark Ages Wraith. Seeing the guilds being active and Charon still be around are the most interesting concepts for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. That alone would be worth it as it most definitely would have a huge impact on the Day to Day &quot;life&quot; of the wraith. And then you also have the rise of Islam during this period...so how did it translate in the Shadowlands? That too could be fun to explore as back in the Skinlands relations we're not always bad (just read on Charlemagne and his Saracean allies).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T20:47:46-08:00","id":1161415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boneguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1160960-who-else-would-love-to-see-dark-age-wraith-dark-age-mummy-become-a-reality?p=1161334#post1161334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly. That alone would be worth it as it most definitely would have a huge impact on the Day to Day &quot;life&quot; of the wraith. And then you also have the rise of Islam during this period...so how did it translate in the Shadowlands? That too could be fun to explore as back in the Skinlands relations we're not always bad (just read on Charlemagne and his Saracean allies).</div> </div> </div> </div>Or how would the Pagan vs Christian skirmishes effect things? Also, how were things between the Wraiths and the Vampires known as the Cappadocians?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T13:49:50-08:00","id":1161604,"title":"","content":"One of the reasons I have long wished Werewolf's historical setting had been the Roman Empire instead of the Wild West - besides the obvious inclusion of the White Howlers - is that you could've had a Necropolis: Stygia book as a crossover/Wraith historical book.<br /> <br /> (And I say this as someone who rather liked WW:WW.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T14:18:21-08:00","id":1161608,"title":"","content":"@Yaoi Huntress Earth.<br /> <br /> I agree, these 2 points would be worth exploring. Especially in regards to the old Wraith that holds true to the Greek or Roman Gods, as well as the Norse Gods, Celtic Gods, etc. And the Cappadocian, good call. Heck even the Tal'MaHe'Ra could be worth looking into.<br /> <br /> @No One of Consequence<br /> <br /> Both your Ashen Lady and Necropolis Stygia/Werewolf Roman Era ideas are excellent. I would definitely go for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":3226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","user":"Boneguard","date":". 11-22-2017, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T15:44:34-08:00","id":1161635,"title":"","content":"Another plus about &quot;Werewolf: Savage Rome&quot; (as I call it), is I can do a book called Amazons that covers women in the period, acts as a Black Furies mini tribe book, and presents legendary badass warrior women as an optional &quot;twilight people&quot; player type. <br /> <br /> Also, &quot;Children of the Gods&quot;, the Changeling crossover book presenting the Fair Folk as strait up Greco-Roman, Germanic and Celtic Gods, with &quot;Changelings&quot; as their demigod hero offspring. <br /> <br /> With Dark Ages: Wraith, I think you could almost do two different but related games, the low-key Shadowlands based dark medieval fantasy thing I described, and this high-powered game of ruthless politics and surreal mysticism with Roman Era survivors of the (First) Great Maelstrom in Stygia and the Tempest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T15:58:52-08:00","id":1161638,"title":"","content":"Those are awesome ideas...you might want to work on them for when the Storyhteller Vaults open up the Werewolf and Changeling option. I'll be buying those (and maybe add my alternate <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes#post354143\">Tribes</a> ideas to the lot).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T18:29:06-08:00","id":1161681,"title":"","content":"On a tangent, the alternate Dark Ages: Werewolf concept I had at the same time required fiddling with the history a bit, particularly with the events involving the Silver Crown. In this alternate setting, House Winter Snow's rise to prominence occurred right after the fall of Rome and the fall from power of House Conquering Claw, so it is at about the end of the 11th century when their leader finds the Silver Crown and turns into a power-mad tyrant king. The game is set a short time after Winter Snow's collapse and failure, and revolves around the power vacuum and chaos they left behind. In effect, the Garou Nation in Europe has fallen into civil war. On one side, your have the forces of the <i>Falcon Banner</i>, Silver Fangs of House Austere Howl (supported by House Crescent Moon, as well as the remains of Conquering Claw and new upstarts Gleaming Eye) and those Garou packs and septs that remain loyal to them. Against them are the <i>Army of Thunder</i>, the Shadow Lords of Hungary and Iberia, and those who believe it is time for a radical change in leadership. And against both of them stands the <i>Unicorn Crusade</i>, lead by the Children of Gaia who believe this is the best chance to force the Garou Nation into unity under their enlightened leadership. The Fianna and Fenrir, both of who took the brunt of Winter Snow's power-madness, are caught in the middle of this mess, along with the Warders, Black Furies, Bone Gnawers, Red Talons, and Silent Striders.<br /> <br /> (The DA:WW Companion would've gone into more detail about the three factions, as well as covering Dark Medieval Europe's Fera - mostly Corax, Ratkin, and Ceilican - and the state of Garou and Fera in the House of Islam, the Medieval Umbra, and various outside threats to the Garou from Wyrm cults and the like.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T09:04:56-08:00","id":1161887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1160960-who-else-would-love-to-see-dark-age-wraith-dark-age-mummy-become-a-reality?p=1161604#post1161604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the reasons I have long wished Werewolf's historical setting had been the Roman Empire instead of the Wild West - besides the obvious inclusion of the White Howlers - is that you could've had a Necropolis: Stygia book as a crossover/Wraith historical book.<br /> <br /> (And I say this as someone who rather liked WW:WW.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Howlers were strictly early empire. They stopped being a thing a bit before 200 CE, so there's a rather large portion of Imperial Roman time where you have BSDs instead. Also, given the attitude of WW at the time, it shouldn't surprise you that they veered away from providing any means of mechanically detailing White Howlers. &quot;Okay, you can play the White Howlers&quot; is strictly a W20 and on development. Before that it was derisive laughter and ignoring pleas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T09:30:59-08:00","id":1161895,"title":"","content":"Well, by Roman Empire, I mean around 100 AD or so, during the &quot;Five Good Emperors&quot;/Antonine Dynasty period. And my thought was that, rather than the regular style clan books that the Cappadocians and Salubri did in V:tDA, they would get a book that was both a tribe book and went into detail about the tribe's fall, how and why it happened, how the other Garou reacted, how to run it as an epic campaign (complete with precursors and foreshadowing during the game's default time period and even do carry over epilogues in Dark Ages, Victorian and modern games) and so forth. <i>The Rise &amp; Fall of the White Howlers</i>, or something like that. <br /> <br /> Also, the signature setting would've been Rage Across Britain, where you'd get to see a fair cross section of them, including interactions with Fianna and Roman influenced Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T10:49:29-08:00","id":1161914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1160960-who-else-would-love-to-see-dark-age-wraith-dark-age-mummy-become-a-reality?p=1161895#post1161895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, by Roman Empire, I mean around 100 AD or so, during the &quot;Five Good Emperors&quot;/Antonine Dynasty period. And my thought was that, rather than the regular style clan books that the Cappadocians and Salubri did in V:tDA, they would get a book that was both a tribe book and went into detail about the tribe's fall, how and why it happened, how the other Garou reacted, how to run it as an epic campaign (complete with precursors and foreshadowing during the game's default time period and even do carry over epilogues in Dark Ages, Victorian and modern games) and so forth. <i>The Rise &amp; Fall of the White Howlers</i>, or something like that.<br /> <br /> Also, the signature setting would've been Rage Across Britain, where you'd get to see a fair cross section of them, including interactions with Fianna and Roman influenced Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>WW tended to prefer settings during a perceived decline rather than one of rising fortunes, though, along with historical upheaval. So it probably would have been the later empire, even before we get into the past need to make sure that no one ever plays a White Howler, at least not with official support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T13:52:28-08:00","id":1161956,"title":"","content":"Yes, but I wanted to set it before the legalization of Christianity, and at what might've been the hight for the Warders and members of House Conquering Claw who'd hitched their wagons to Rome's fortunes, at the expense of those Garou who are more aligned with the &quot;barbarian&quot; tribes. And allowing people to actually play White Howlers - in the same way that V:tDA allowed you to play the doomed Cappadocians (and IMO should've included the equally doomed Salubri as part of the core book) - because it works as one of the selling points for the line and, in the case of Werewolf, playing one of the first Tribes to fall and knowing that your character is doomed from the start ties into one of Werewolf's main themes of being part of a dying race raging against inevitable extinction.<br /> <br /> My theoretical line up for said line would've been:<br /> <br /> [*=1]\u200bWerewolf: Savage Rome corebook (with the Black Furies, Bone Gnawers, Children of Gaia, Fianna, Fenrir, Red Talons, Shadow Lords, Silent Striders, Silver Fangs (focused on Conquering Claw), Warders, and White Howlers)<br /> [*=1]Secrets of the Ancient World (with the Storytellers Screen, including notes on Stargazers, Fera and other odds and ends)<br /> [*=1]Rage Across Britain<br /> [*=1]Gods &amp; Monsters (a collection of antagonists and other dangers, including other supernaturals, the forces of the Triat, and human threats)<br /> [*=1]Savage Rome Companion (more on the Fera, life in the 1st century, the ancient Umbra)<br /> [*=1]White Howlers (as discussed above)<br /> [*=1]Rome: The Conquering Claw (a guide to the Roman Empire and the Garou who've adapted to it)<br /> [*=1]Barbarians: The Savage Hordes (a guide to the Celtic, Germanic, Slavic and other tribes outside of &quot;civilization&quot; and the Garou among them)<br /> [*=1]Savage Rome by Night (a look at the city of Rome and a Vampire crossover sourcebook)<br /> [*=1]Gladiators (what they are, when Garou and other supernaturals become one, and running chronicles around the arena)<br /> [*=1]Savage Sands (Egypt)<br /> [*=1]Legion of the Sun Bull (about the militant Mitras cult that hunts supernatural monsters and demons)<br /> [*=1]Arcana Roma: Magic of Rome (a look at period magic and a Mage crossover sourcebook)<br /> [*=1]Amazons (see above)<br /> [*=1]Ancient Beasts (a collection of powerful monsters, some still existing into the modern nights)<br /> [*=1](Book about the East - Persia, India and China)<br /> [*=1]Necropolis: Stygia (the Wraith crossover sourcebook and look at the Dark Umbra)<br /> [*=1]Byzantine Moon (about the Eastern Roman Empire near the end of the ancient period and how to use it as a bridge into the Dark Ages setting)<br /> [*=1]Kingdoms of the Jaguar (a sort of stand alone historical sourcebook about Fera and Garou in the late preclassical Mayan civilization)<br /> [*=1]Soothsayers (about prophecy, including the Prophecy of the Phoenix, and how to incorporate them into a chronicle, as well as offering them as a PC type)<br /> [*=1]Children of the Gods (the Changeling crossover book)<br /> [*=1]The Black Spiral (a guide to Wyrm cults and other forces of the corruptor)<br /> [*=1]Age's End: Darkness Falls (about the end of the western Empire, the fall out of the loss of the White Howlers, and the collapse of House Conquering Claw)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 11-23-2017, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T14:12:28-08:00","id":1161964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1160960-who-else-would-love-to-see-dark-age-wraith-dark-age-mummy-become-a-reality?p=1161681#post1161681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(The DA:WW Companion would've gone into more detail about the three factions, as well as covering Dark Medieval Europe's Fera - mostly Corax, Ratkin, and Ceilican - and the state of Garou and Fera in the House of Islam, the Medieval Umbra, and various outside threats to the Garou from Wyrm cults and the like.)</div> </div> </div> </div>that's another book I'mm pretty sad never got published. Medieval Europe Get a would have been awesome to look into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T14:42:29-08:00","id":1161972,"title":"","content":"I was honestly a little shocked that there wasn't a Dark Ages: Werewolf Companion book to go along with the Mage and Inquisitor ones. I mean, between the medieval Umbra and the period Fera, there's all these little things like what the Silver Fang House politics situation was, how the Black Furies dealt with the role of women and the Catholic Church, what the medieval Warders were like as compared to the modern Glasswalkers, the non-extinction oriented mindset of the Red Talons, the Shadow Lords using the Reconquista as a way to seize territory in Iberia, and how and why Stargazers might actually show up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T15:18:59-08:00","id":1161980,"title":"","content":"Dark Age Werewolf and Dark Age Fae deserved a Companion book...the same way Mummy the Ressurection and Wraith the Oblivion deserved a Dark Age book.<br /> <br /> Plus back I Medieval time, aurochs we still around, they went extinct in the early 1600. How did the Garou felt about those living reminder of the Apis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T18:19:49-08:00","id":1162305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boneguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1160960-who-else-would-love-to-see-dark-age-wraith-dark-age-mummy-become-a-reality?p=1161980#post1161980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dark Age Werewolf and Dark Age Fae deserved a Companion book...the same way Mummy the Ressurection and Wraith the Oblivion deserved a Dark Age book.<br /> <br /> Plus back I Medieval time, aurochs we still around, they went extinct in the early 1600. How did the Garou felt about those living reminder of the Apis?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most Garou probably wouldn't have known. By the time the 13th century rolled around, even the fall of the White Howlers was ancient history. Whatever happened during the War of Rage was even foggier to the vast majority of anyone who hadn't learned vast amounts of the Silver Record in great detail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T19:18:13-08:00","id":1164144,"title":"","content":"If I recall correctly, the Fishers were still active in Stygia during the period covered by the Dark Ages. <br /> <br /> As well, Dark Ages predates the Second Great Maelstrom (which coincides with the Black Death a few centuries later). Think of what that means: the phenomenon of the Great Maelstrom has only happened <i>once</i>; and as devastating as that was, nobody has any reason to think it might happen again \u2014 let alone five more times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" ta